meta {
  name: Smoke Test Remaining Attribute Types
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "wc_test_multiline",
    "type": "MultilineAttribute"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". Per
  `TESTING_PLAN.md` 1d, the remaining 10 attribute types (beyond
  `TextAttribute`/`DropdownAttribute`/`FormulaAttribute`/`MediaAttribute`,
  each covered in their own file) were smoke-tested with a minimal
  `{name, type}` body each (plus `options` for `MultiSelectAttribute`,
  which requires at least the array to be meaningful). All 9 real types
  below created successfully (`201`) and were deleted again in the same
  test run (none are Phase 2b dependents):

  | Type | Created id (deleted) | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | `MultilineAttribute` | `6a9f1c062b6fd055ffb7c7e7` | base request above |
  | `BooleanAttribute` | `6a9f1c062b6fd055ffb7c7e9` | no extra fields |
  | `DateAttribute` | `6a9f1c072b6fd055ffb7c7eb` | `include_time` defaults `false` |
  | `DecimalAttribute` | `6a9f1c072b6fd055ffb7c7ed` | no extra fields |
  | `HtmlAttribute` | `6a9f1c082b6fd055ffb7c7ef` | no extra fields |
  | `IntAttribute` | `6a9f1c092b6fd055ffb7c7f1` | no extra fields |
  | `MediaGalleryAttribute` | `6a9f1c092b6fd055ffb7c7f3` | no extra fields |
  | `UrlAttribute` | `6a9f1c0a2b6fd055ffb7c7f5` | no extra fields |
  | `MultiSelectAttribute` | `6a9f1c0a2b6fd055ffb7c7f7` | same defaulting as `DropdownAttribute` (`manual_sorting`/`sort_ascending`/`restricted`) |
  | `CompletenessAttribute` | `6a9f1c0b2b6fd055ffb7c7f9` | `attributes` defaults to `[]`; not tested with a real referenced-attributes list |

  ## Undocumented 15th type found -- flag to Plytix
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `POST /product-attributes` `oneOf` declares only
  **14** types (matches `TESTING_PLAN.md`'s list). But triggering a 422
  with an invalid `type` value returns an error message naming **15**
  valid discriminator tags -- including **`HierarchyAttribute`**, which
  appears nowhere in the spec. See "Create Attribute - Invalid Type (422,
  Lists Undocumented Type).bru" and "Create Attribute -
  HierarchyAttribute (500, Unimplemented).bru" in this folder for the
  full detail -- attempting to actually create one 500s, suggesting it's
  a real but unfinished/unexposed feature, not documentation-ready.
}
